177	            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
178	        OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
179	        headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
180	            .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
181	        return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
182	    }
183	
184	    /**
185	     * Enforces the pre-persistence policies that reject a newly mapped and normalized owner
186	     * outright, in order, before any derived fields are assigned or the owner is saved. An owner
187	     * in a city that already contains {@link #MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY} owners is rejected with 409
188	     * ({@link CityCapacityExceededException}), and an owner whose normalized telephone is already
189	     * used by another owner is rejected with 409 ({@link DuplicateTelephoneException}). Grouping the
190	     * independent create-time rejection rules here keeps {@link #addOwner} focused on the household,
191	     * derived-field and persistence steps. The household rule stays in {@link #addOwner} itself
192	     * because it shares the matched-member lookup with the shared household-id assignment.
193	     *
194	     * @param owner the newly mapped and normalized owner being created
195	     */
196	    private void rejectDisallowedOwnerCreation(Owner owner) {
197	        // Reject creating an owner once 100 or more owners already carry this owner's adjusted
198	        // business-day registration date.
199	        if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(owner.getRegistrationDate()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
200	            throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(
201	                "The maximum number of owners that may be created today has already been reached");
202	        }
203	        // Reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.
204	        if (countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) {
205	            throw new CityCapacityExceededException(
206	                "The city " + owner.getCity() + " already contains the maximum number of owners");
207	        }
208	        // Reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by another owner.
209	        String normalizedTelephone = owner.getTelephone();
210	        if (isTelephoneInUse(normalizedTelephone)) {
211	            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(
212	                "An owner with telephone " + normalizedTelephone + " already exists");
213	        }
214	    }
215	
216	    /**
217	     * Canonicalizes the fields of a newly mapped owner on create, in place, so each value is
218	     * persisted and returned in its canonical form. The address is normalized (trimmed, whitespace
219	     * collapsed, upper-cased and common abbreviations expanded, rejecting a value blank after
220	     * normalization with 400), the telephone is normalized to E.164 (rejecting an unformattable
221	     * value with 400), the email is lower-cased, and a missing registration date defaults to the
222	     * server's current date. Canonicalising the address here, before the household checks read it,
223	     * ensures duplicate detection and the shared household id both compare the normalized form.
224	     * Centralising these per-field canonicalizations here keeps {@link #addOwner} focused on the
225	     * duplicate, household and customer-code rules.
226	     *
227	     * @param owner the newly mapped owner to canonicalize
228	     */
229	    private void normalizeOwnerFields(Owner owner) {
230	        // Normalize the address on create so it is stored and returned in canonical form and every
231	        // later comparison (household duplicate detection and the shared household id) uses it.
232	        // A value that is blank after normalization is rejected with 400.
233	        owner.setAddress(addressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress()));
234	        // Normalize the telephone on create so it is stored and returned in canonical E.164 form.
235	        // A value that cannot form a valid E.164 number is rejected with 400.
236	        owner.setTelephone(telephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone()));
237	        // Store the (already syntactically validated) email lower-cased so it is persisted and
238	        // returned in canonical form. A missing email is left untouched.
239	        owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
240	        // Default the registration date to the server's current date when the client did not
241	        // supply one, then roll the effective date forward to a business day so a Saturday or
242	        // Sunday (whether supplied or defaulted) becomes the following Monday. The adjusted date
243	        // is persisted and returned in ISO 'YYYY-MM-DD' form and is the value every registration-
244	        // date-derived field (such as the membership number's year segment) and the per-day
245	        // create-limit are computed from.
246	        java.time.LocalDate effectiveDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() == null
247	            ? java.time.LocalDate.now() : owner.getRegistrationDate();
248	        owner.setRegistrationDate(toBusinessDay(effectiveDate));
249	    }
250	
251	    /**
252	     * Rolls a registration date forward to a business day: a Saturday or Sunday advances to the
253	     * following Monday, while a weekday is returned unchanged. Applied to the effective
254	     * registration date (whether supplied in the request or defaulted to the server date) so the
255	     * persisted registration date, every value derived from it and the per-day create-limit all
256	     * use the adjusted business day.
257	     *
258	     * @param date the effective registration date
259	     * @return the same date if it is a weekday, otherwise the following Monday
260	     */
261	    private java.time.LocalDate toBusinessDay(java.time.LocalDate date) {
262	        java.time.LocalDate adjusted = date;
263	        while (adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == java.time.DayOfWeek.SATURDAY
264	            || adjusted.getDayOfWeek() == java.time.DayOfWeek.SUNDAY) {
265	            adjusted = adjusted.plusDays(1);
266	        }
267	        return adjusted;
268	    }
269	
270	    /**
271	     * Lower-cases the supplied email address so it is stored and returned in canonical form.
272	     * Bean validation on the request DTO has already guaranteed that any non-null value is a
273	     * syntactically valid address (rejecting anything else with 400).
274	     *
275	     * @param email the email value (may be {@code null})
276	     * @return the lower-cased email, or {@code null} if the input was {@code null}
277	     */
278	    private String normalizeEmail(String email) {
279	        return email == null ? null : email.toLowerCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT);
280	    }
281	
282	    /**
283	     * Builds the customer code '<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>' for a newly created owner, where CITY3 is
284	     * the upper-cased first three letters of the city, LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters
285	     * of the last name and NNNN is a per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than
286	     * the owners already in that city (e.g. 'LON-SMI-0007').
287	     *
288	     * @param city     the owner's city
289	     * @param lastName the owner's last name
290	     * @return the formatted customer code
291	     */
292	    private String nextCustomerCode(String city, String lastName) {
293	        String cityPrefix = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length()))
294	            .toUpperCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT);
295	        String lastPrefix = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length()))
296	            .toUpperCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT);
297	        int sequence = countOwnersInCity(city) + 1;
298	        return String.format("%s-%s-%04d", cityPrefix, lastPrefix, sequence);
299	    }
300	
301	    /**
302	     * Counts the existing owners located in the given city, compared case-insensitively. Used to
303	     * fix the per-city sequence of an owner's customer code at creation time.
304	     *
305	     * @param city the city of the owner being created
306	     * @return the number of existing owners in a matching city
307	     */
308	    private int countOwnersInCity(String city) {
309	        return (int) this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
310	            .filter(existing -> existing.getCity() != null
311	                && existing.getCity().equalsIgnoreCase(city))
312	            .count();
313	    }
314	
315	    /**
316	     * Counts the existing owners whose registration date is the given adjusted business day. Used
317	     * to enforce the per-day cap that rejects creating an owner once {@link #MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY}
318	     * owners already carry that business day as their registration date.
319	     *
320	     * @param date the adjusted business-day registration date to match
321	     * @return the number of existing owners registered on that date
322	     */
323	    private int countOwnersRegisteredOn(java.time.LocalDate date) {
324	        return (int) this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
325	            .filter(existing -> date.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))
326	            .count();
327	    }
328	
329	    /**
330	     * Builds the membership number '<customerCode>-M<YY>' for a newly created owner, where YY is
331	     * the last two digits of the registration date's year (e.g. 'LON-SMI-0007-M26').
332	     *
333	     * @param customerCode     the owner's customer code
334	     * @param registrationDate the owner's registration date
335	     * @return the formatted membership number
336	     */
337	    private String membershipNumber(String customerCode, java.time.LocalDate registrationDate) {
338	        return String.format("%s-M%02d", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
339	    }
340	
341	    /**
342	     * Determines whether the given normalized telephone is already used by an existing owner.
343	     * Stored telephones are normalized to E.164 before comparison so values that differ only in
344	     * formatting (spaces, dashes, brackets) or in national vs. international notation are treated
345	     * as the same number.
346	     *
347	     * @param normalizedTelephone the normalized (E.164) telephone to look for
348	     * @return {@code true} if another owner already uses this telephone
349	     */
350	    private boolean isTelephoneInUse(String normalizedTelephone) {
351	        if (normalizedTelephone == null) {
352	            return false;
353	        }
354	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
355	            .map(Owner::getTelephone)
356	            .map(telephoneNormalizer::normalize)
357	            .anyMatch(normalizedTelephone::equals);
358	    }
359	
360	    /**
361	     * Returns the existing owners who share the given household, i.e. have the same last name and
362	     * the same address. The comparison delegates to {@link HouseholdNormalizer} so that values
363	     * differing only in letter case or in incidental whitespace are treated as the same household.
364	     *
365	     * @param lastName the last name of the owner being created
366	     * @param address  the address of the owner being created
367	     * @return the existing owners with a matching last name and address (possibly empty)
368	     */
369	    private List<Owner> sameHouseholdOwners(String lastName, String address) {
370	        String householdKey = householdNormalizer.householdKey(lastName, address);
371	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
372	            .filter(existing -> householdNormalizer
373	                .householdKey(existing.getLastName(), existing.getAddress()).equals(householdKey))
374	            .toList();
375	    }
376	
377	    /**
378	     * Counts the existing owners who share the given first and last name, compared
379	     * case-insensitively. Used to fix an owner's namesake count at creation time.
380	     *
381	     * @param firstName the first name of the owner being created
382	     * @param lastName  the last name of the owner being created
383	     * @return the number of existing owners with a matching first and last name
384	     */
385	    private int countNamesakes(String firstName, String lastName) {
386	        return (int) this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
387	            .filter(existing -> existing.getFirstName() != null
388	                && existing.getFirstName().equalsIgnoreCase(firstName)
389	                && existing.getLastName() != null
390	                && existing.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(lastName))
391	            .count();
392	    }
393	
394	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
395	    @Override
396	    public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> updateOwner(Integer ownerId, OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
397	        Owner currentOwner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(ownerId);
398	        if (currentOwner == null) {
399	            return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
400	        }
401	        currentOwner.setAddress(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress());
402	        currentOwner.setCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
403	        currentOwner.setFirstName(ownerFieldsDto.getFirstName());
404	        currentOwner.setLastName(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName());
405	        // Normalize the telephone to canonical E.164 form so it is stored and returned
406	        // consistently with create; an unformattable value is rejected with 400.
407	        currentOwner.setTelephone(telephoneNormalizer.normalize(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone()));
408	        currentOwner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(ownerFieldsDto.getEmail()));
409	        this.clinicService.saveOwner(currentOwner);
410	        return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(currentOwner), HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT);
411	    }
412	
413	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
414	    @Transactional
415	    @Override
416	    public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> deleteOwner(Integer ownerId) {
417	        Owner owner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(ownerId);
418	        if (owner == null) {
419	            return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
420	        }
421	        this.clinicService.deleteOwner(owner);
422	        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT);
423	    }
424	
425	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
426	    @Override
427	    public ResponseEntity<PetDto> addPetToOwner(Integer ownerId, PetFieldsDto petFieldsDto) {
428	        Owner owner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(ownerId);
429	        if (owner == null) {
430	            return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
431	        }
432	        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
433	        Pet pet = petMapper.toPet(petFieldsDto);
434	        owner.setId(ownerId);
435	        pet.setOwner(owner);
436	        pet.getType().setName(null);
437	        this.clinicService.savePet(pet);
438	        PetDto petDto = petMapper.toPetDto(pet);
439	        headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance().path("/api/pets/{id}")
440	            .buildAndExpand(pet.getId()).toUri());
441	        return new ResponseEntity<>(petDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
442	    }
443	
444	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
445	    @Override
446	    public ResponseEntity<Void> updateOwnersPet(Integer ownerId, Integer petId, PetFieldsDto petFieldsDto) {
447	        Owner currentOwner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(ownerId);
448	        if (currentOwner != null) {
449	            Pet currentPet = this.clinicService.findPetById(petId);
450	            if (currentPet != null) {
451	                currentPet.setBirthDate(petFieldsDto.getBirthDate());
452	                currentPet.setName(petFieldsDto.getName());
453	                currentPet.setType(petMapper.toPetType(petFieldsDto.getType()));
454	                this.clinicService.savePet(currentPet);
455	                return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT);
456	            }
457	        }
458	        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
459	    }
460	
461	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
462	    @Override
463	    public ResponseEntity<VisitDto> addVisitToOwner(Integer ownerId, Integer petId, VisitFieldsDto visitFieldsDto) {
464	        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
465	        Visit visit = visitMapper.toVisit(visitFieldsDto);
466	        Pet pet = new Pet();
467	        pet.setId(petId);
468	        visit.setPet(pet);
469	        this.clinicService.saveVisit(visit);
470	        VisitDto visitDto = visitMapper.toVisitDto(visit);
471	        headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance().path("/api/visits/{id}")
472	            .buildAndExpand(visit.getId()).toUri());
473	        return new ResponseEntity<>(visitDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
474	    }
475	
476	
477	    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
478	    @Override
479	    public ResponseEntity<PetDto> getOwnersPet(Integer ownerId, Integer petId) {
480	        Owner owner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(ownerId);
481	        if (owner != null) {
482	            Pet pet = owner.getPet(petId);
483	            if (pet != null) {
484	                return new ResponseEntity<>(petMapper.toPetDto(pet), HttpStatus.OK);
485	            }
486	        }
487	        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
488	    }
489	}
